Evidence boundary
-----------------
The native notice checker verifies the recorded notice-file set and SHA-256
values, zlib configuration, Tauri CLI version and selected WebView2 binding
version. Collection additionally checks the installed NSIS version, plugin
asset digest and supplied SDK archive/library digests.

Those checks do not prove final installer contents, successful installation,
the final executable import table, code-signing status or a complete prebuilt
dependency SBOM. Final packaging must carry LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES, this
file and the original notice directories; artifact and installed-file checks
remain separate evidence. The recorded toolchain and component versions must be
reviewed when the build environment changes.
